WEBVTT

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.330
Whassup?

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.010
Did you see that yesterday?

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:45.040
I did!  It was like, totally freaky.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.960
Do you really think something like that exists?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.660
No way.  Not a chance, right?

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.170
I wouldn't believe it!

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.210
But there were people who saw it...

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:56.920
Isn't that just one of those Tokyo stories?

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.230
But the teacher, see...

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.230
Really?

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:02.300
He said it was true.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.600
Crap...

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:40.290
Thank... you...

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.610
See you!

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:03.650
I was shunned again.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.980
Why?

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:09.790
Maybe I should have tried to strike up a conversation.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:16.110
But I'm no good at talking, and I can never across what I'm trying to say.

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:16.750
Interpersonal Relationships
Beginner Level

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:20.000
If they misunderstand it'll be a real problem.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.410
But I'm reading this book.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:28.980
I did just what it says.  I made sure I was smiling properly.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.980
I did smile correctly, right?

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:44.080
Look, Tsubomiya is grinning while reading that book.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.370
Freaky...

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.330
My cellphone...

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:03.180
The only numbers I have saved in my cellphone are my family's.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.250
Are you kiddin' me?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.380
Sorry, I lost my footing there.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:22.440
Sorry 'bout that.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:28.120
Kageyama Torako-san...

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.100
See ya.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.390
Kageyama Torako-san.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:18.010
She's amazing.

00:05:18.690 --> 00:05:23.260
She's so outspoken, and I bet she has a lot of friends.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:37.940
I wonder what it's like to have friends?

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:42.360
What's that?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.950
It seems like world far out of my reach...

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:00.540
How should I make friends?

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.430
I just don't know!

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:08.190
Oh, God!  If I was able to speak like that...

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:14.100
No, that's why I'm no good.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:20.920
If I don't do it now, I'll never make a friend my entire life!

00:06:23.140 --> 00:06:24.150
That's it!

00:06:24.490 --> 00:06:28.110
First, I'll try and make Kageyama-san my friend.

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:32.010
If it's her... If it's her, then surely...

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:37.580
Lalala... Dog fight!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:44.370
Rip off, rip off a dog's tail...

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:50.010
Huh?  Maybe those were the lyrics to #2?

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.370
And I get my big chance just like this?!

00:06:55.370 --> 00:07:00.230
Yeah, but... I haven't mentally prepared myself!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:04.070
Ah, I forgot my handkerchief.

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:05.550
Like, seriously?

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.260
Now it's a double chance!

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.690
Should I offer her my handkerchief?

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:16.740
God!  I'll do it!  Just watch!

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:25.710
Did you say something?

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:29.590
Um...  Um...

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:33.920
Han?

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.970
Han... Haka...

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:47.440
Haka?  Grave?!

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.440
Note:  Haka means "grave"

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.650
Hanker... chi...

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:56.030
Note:  "Chi" means blood.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.650
B-Blood?!

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:56.030
What's with this person?

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:59.740
Um, maybe I should go...

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.650
Don't go, Kageyama-san!

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.040
You still haven't wiped your hands!

00:08:07.060 --> 00:08:08.710
You can't leave!

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.760
Why?  Who is she?

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:32.030
It'll all be over s-soon, so...

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:35.240
What's going on?  What is she going to do to me?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.910
Rip it off...

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:42.790
Suzu?

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.510
STOP!

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.360
What're you doing?

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:09.300
Torako, you'll be dead after a week!

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:16.340
Well, she does kind of look similar, but...

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:20.780
But I don't think that's her.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.060
Probably...

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.950
You sure you're okay?

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:31.450
Y-Yes...

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.270
I'm sorry, Sadako!

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.620
Hey!  Don't go calling her that!

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:42.460
So what did you want anyway?

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:47.390
Nevermind, it's okay.

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.610
Um...

00:09:54.230 --> 00:09:59.410
Would you mind sharing your cellphone number with me?

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.080
No?  It's okay...

00:10:06.460 --> 00:10:07.740
That's fine.

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.270
I'll add yours, okay?

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.100
Sure.

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.680
Tsubomiya Inori.

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.400
Can I call you Ino?

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:38.570
Ino?

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:40.390
Right, Ino.

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:42.370
P-P-Please do!

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:52.040
Suzu, you won't give her yours?

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:55.250
You won't curse me?

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.760
She's still freaked out.

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.800
Hurry up and deny it!

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:06.640
S-Sure...

00:11:08.090 --> 00:11:11.940
I would never curse my... friends.

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:17.510
So you won't deny that you'd curse people in general?

00:11:17.510 --> 00:11:18.690
Which means, you can?!

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.010
I just totally set up that punch line for them.

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.160
It's almost like we're comedy duo pals!

00:11:24.460 --> 00:11:30.350
You're telling me that there are fifth graders who still believe that made-up story?

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:35.130
So you're not scared of being cursed by ghosts and stuff, Inagi-chan?

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.590
Nope.  Not at all.

00:11:37.590 --> 00:11:40.040
The thing I'm scared of is...

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:43.840
What?

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:49.050
That one day I'll cease being a little girl.

00:11:50.590 --> 00:11:53.520
Maybe that's a curse that's cast upon all little girls?

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:58.610
That's just a line you read in that book before, isn't it?

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.610
We're on next, Ayumi.

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.960
Maybe it's because of how she wears her hair?

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:18.600
She does not spend much time on it, that is for certain.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.380
I don't really know.

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:24.260
Does anyone have any hair bands or pins?

00:12:32.450 --> 00:12:36.930
The reason you can't make any friends is because of your appearance.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:39.190
That's why it's so hard to approach you.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.630
Understand, Ino?

00:12:42.630 --> 00:12:43.860
Ino...

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:47.200
If you want to make a lot of friends, you've got to take better care of yourself!

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.160
Right!

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.390
Koma-san...

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:54.520
Do you have any hairpins or hair bands?

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:58.830
Yep.  I have some.  What are you doing?

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:03.510
Looks like their doin' something interesting.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:06.470
First we've got to get rid of this pesky bangs.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:13.050
Hey!  Stop moving!

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:14.890
We'll just part these a little and...

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.590
I think...

00:13:20.590 --> 00:13:21.950
...that we've...

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:24.440
...got something we can work with here.

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:26.530
Let's tie them back for now.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.360
In the back?  Or the sides?

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.910
I have wax and stuff, too.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.330
Wax?

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.860
This might do it.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:36.790
Not scary.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:38.120
Oh, that's right.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:44.150
Touma!

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.490
Let me borrow your glasses!

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.740
No way!

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:51.470
What's the matter?  It's not such a big deal.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.080
Touma, you're lame!

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:55.780
Chie!

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:56.640
Yes?

00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:58.510
Let me borrow your glasses.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.680
What are you doing?

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:02.470
Give them back!

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:04.980
Give me back my glasses!

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:07.240
Hey, wait!

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.550
Huh?

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.030
I can't see!

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.670
Doesn't that look good?

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:17.830
Think so?

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:21.720
I think we've really brightened up your look.

00:14:21.720 --> 00:14:25.420
But it still doesn't shine out at me...

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:28.670
Doesn't shine, you say?

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:34.640
Seems like we have a difficult case here.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.390
It's not your fault, Tsubomiya-san.

00:14:38.550 --> 00:14:41.030
So please don't feel so down on yourself.

00:14:41.030 --> 00:14:42.140
Um...

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:42.980
What is it?

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:45.150
Call me...

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.950
Don't call me Tsubomiya-san, call me Ino.

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:53.780
I-Ino?

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:55.950
Yes!

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:58.410
That's a nice smile.

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:02.600
Just stay like that a little longer.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:03.620
Right.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.560
How about if we bend this over here?

00:15:09.250 --> 00:15:11.220
That would not be half bad, no?

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:15.040
What are you doing, Torako-san?

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:16.720
When they're done, let's put these on her.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.560
Glasses?  Whose are they?

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:24.410
Wax!

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:28.300
Ushio!

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:30.740
Hold still for a sec!

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:31.620
What for?

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:32.770
Nevermind that.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:34.780
Nevermind what?  Hey!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:37.670
If you're gonna be a punk, it's gotta be...

00:15:40.240 --> 00:15:41.210
It totally suits you!

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.130
What happened to you, Ushio?

00:15:48.370 --> 00:15:50.300
What kind of thing is that on your head?

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.460
You gotta problem with it, bub?!

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.240
Hey!

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.520
Touma!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.990
Wait!

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.000
Oh, Touma!

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:14.570
What's with her?

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:19.000
Torako-san...

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.440
Just hold still now, dear.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:37.020
Huh?  Suzume-san, when did you...

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:56.280
My masterpiece is finished!

00:16:57.430 --> 00:16:59.590
Tatsun, when did you...

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:02.950
So, how'd it turn out?

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:04.870
You guys too?

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:33.630
How do I look?

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:35.420
Great!  Great!

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:37.820
You could even make a hundred friends now, no sweat!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.820
R-Really?

00:17:39.820 --> 00:17:40.820
Yeah!

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:45.220
Hey you!  You're a student, right?  Where'd you come from?

00:17:45.220 --> 00:17:46.670
You're cute!

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.130
Hey!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.560
Tsubomiya-kun?!

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:51.290
You're like a totally different person!

00:17:51.290 --> 00:17:53.400
Wait, I mean this in all seriousness:

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:54.500
I love you!

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.380
For God's sake man, save yourself a little!

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.380
What's with you, Nene?

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:02.430
Have you tossed me aside?

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.140
K-Kageyama-kun!

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:07.530
You're my number one, of course!

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:10.430
You jerk, you silly little jerk...

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:14.460
What's this?

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:15.540
So?

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:16.820
Fantastic!

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.510
Um, my glasses...

00:19:02.900 --> 00:19:04.070
Pardon me...

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.670
Got some business with me?

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.440
No, nothing in particular...

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:14.420
Then don't show up here if I don't call you.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:16.250
Oh, yeah?

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.210
What the hell are you doing?

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:21.890
So, how'd you like it, sir?

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:24.680
Just a bit of a trim off the ends.

00:19:40.990 --> 00:19:42.310
Sensei, what's that?

00:19:42.310 --> 00:19:43.420
What?

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:46.060
That.  What is it?

00:19:46.060 --> 00:19:48.170
It's your quizzes from earlier.

00:19:48.170 --> 00:19:49.600
You got a 45.

00:19:56.410 --> 00:19:59.020
Your scalp is really tight, Sensei.

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:00.980
You'll go bald, I bet.

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:03.720
Really?  Ah, well...

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:06.430
Now then...

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:11.810
Okay, everyone.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.790
We're gonna start where we left off last time.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.070
Let's go to the library.

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:26.410
You don't have a club meeting today?

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:27.990
Are you kidding me?

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:29.580
I've been waiting!

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:31.490
Let me see your notes!

00:20:31.490 --> 00:20:35.710
Hey, can I have my glasses back now?

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.000
Just a little longer.

00:20:43.190 --> 00:20:46.790
Let's make a lot of friends tomorrow!

00:20:46.790 --> 00:20:49.310
Right!  I'll do my best!

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.360
One day and she's right back to where she started.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.480
What happened?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.960
Well, I...

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:12.710
I've never made myself up before, and I tried doing it myself, but...

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.830
I wasn't able to do... do it right...

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.840
We get it, don't cry!

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.970
We'll do you up again, don't worry.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:21.130
This's gonna get annoying.

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:23.300
Good morning!

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:29.480
So, shall we begin?

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:31.600
Why did he leave it like that?

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:38.610
And he even improved on it!

00:21:45.310 --> 00:21:47.010
Say something, damn you!

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:48.560
You totally spoiled my setup!

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:22.030
So, what's on next week's Hyakko?

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:24.960
"Pity, not for the Tiger's Sake.  Suzume and you Shall Receive."

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:25.800
It's two stories!

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:30.720
"Pity, not for the sake of man" means that kindness done to people will eventually be repaid, right?

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:32.560
Doesn't it mean not to spoil people?

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:34.090
Tune in next time!
